1
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,920
kicking a pebble, flying along

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,360
to the Kashiwa type who was out jogging

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed that you'd stay
just as full of energy as ever.

5
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:36,140
Where's the good energy?

6
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,680
As a man, too,
there's a gutsy spirit to hold on to.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare, the streets that never change,

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
are gentler somehow.

9
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:48,700
the sun has already gone down.

11
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:53,860
Yakitori, honbari... are you having some?

12
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:11,220
Thank you for watching.

13
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:27,540
Papa, the young camping champ

14
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:30,640
What?

15
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,500
Don't be so surprised.

16
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:36,960
You're joking, Terai.

17
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:39,960
Yoisho! Terai-san goes outdoors,

18
00:01:40,580 --> 00:01:42,660
even you, Nakagawa-kun? That's hurtful.

19
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:45,260
Camping: just wing it and see.

20
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:46,760
Where there's a will,
there's a way outdoors.

21
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:48,700
Auto camping, even you can do it.

22
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:50,540
Terai-san seems serious, doesn't he?

23
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:51,900
Of course I'm serious.

24
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:54,940
We made a promise, after all.

25
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,940
There's no cell reception
way out in these mountains.

26
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:14,100
And you can't play video games either.
Is that okay?

27
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:16,420
Yeah, it's super fun!

28
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:18,180
I caught this many fish!

29
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:21,120
Enjoying camping in nature,

30
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,900
deepening family bonds.

31
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:29,940
Look at that. Friends are going to a campsite with their families,
so it's camping

32
00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:36,440
We're not going anywhere again this summer break, are we?
Maybe I'll write a diary as if I'd gone.

33
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:41,340
Big brother, you're so smart!
I'll do that too. I'll take you camping.

34
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:42,720
Really?

35
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:47,220
Let's go camping and make
summer vacation memories!

36
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:49,580
We're going to make memories.

37
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:53,100
Making summer vacation memories

38
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:56,440
Taking this chance to show
off the father's legacy,

39
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:59,480
maybe the kids will think better of me too.

40
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:03,220
Terai-san,
do you have any auto camping experience?

41
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,280
Not at all, actually.

42
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:08,900
But I can't let the kids see me look uncool,
you know.

43
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:12,640
Actually, I was hoping Ryo-san
would teach me a few things.

44
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:13,920
I was counting on you, you know.

45
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:17,680
Relying on others,
what kind of dignity is that for a father?

46
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:20,640
All you'll end up with
is your kid's bad mood.

47
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:22,540
Don't do it, don't do it.

48
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,080
Ryo-san,

49
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:26,860
don't be so mean, why not coach him?

50
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,540
That's right, senpai.

51
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:32,860
The outdoor leisure knowledge
I've built up over many years

52
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,760
you want me to hand over
to this guy for free?

53
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,180
No way.

54
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,520
Ryo-chan's isn't leisure,

55
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:40,160
it's survival knowledge.

56
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:41,740
All the more reason not to.

57
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:44,680
It's the crystallization of my blood,
sweat, and hunger.

58
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:47,640
Of course,
I've thought about a fitting thank-you.

59
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:50,900
Terai, the "Life Sender," is thinking

60
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:53,460
that any reasonable
thank-you is pretty meager.

61
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:56,620
How about ten days'
worth of my wife's bento?

62
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:58,160
See?

63
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:00,780
Of course that's fine, right, Ryo-chan?

64
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:03,720
Well, you saved on lunch money, didn't you?

65
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:07,980
Well, Terai's wife's bento is plain,
but it's delicious.

66
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:11,160
Then I'll give you fourteen
days' worth of bento.

67
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:13,580
By the way, didn't you have a car?

68
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:14,360
A car?

69
00:04:15,740 --> 00:04:17,440
I have a Subaru R2.

70
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:20,660
That's been your car for over forty years!

71
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:21,720
And it's a kei car.

72
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:24,220
And it can't carry much luggage.

73
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:25,920
With four family members,

74
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:27,880
would that be too much?

75
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:31,460
At the very least,
it needs to be four-wheel drive.

76
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:34,060
Buy a new car! A man should buy a new car!

77
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:43,060
That's amazing.

78
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:48,260
For a family of four,
I'd say there's plenty of room.

79
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,400
Yeah, and the kitchen is spacious too.

80
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:53,460
It even has a toilet and a shower.

81
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:55,240
Nice, it looks great.

82
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:57,280
The kids will be thrilled, I bet.

83
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:59,900
Your dad's reputation will shoot right up.

84
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:00,960
I guarantee it.

85
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:07,620
So, how much is it?
The current discounted price is...

86
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:11,120
It's 13 million yen. 13 million.

87
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:16,160
Of course, we can arrange a loan too,
over 30 years, that works, right?

88
00:05:17,220 --> 00:05:20,400
A 30-year loan? Please wait a moment.

89
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:27,020
I never thought I'd take out a 30-year loan just to go camping.
Auto camping, no less.

90
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:29,580
Give up on the loan.
If you're going to run away, now's the time.

91
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:32,300
This is where I should take the plunge.

92
00:05:32,350 --> 00:05:34,660
But I still have the house loan.

93
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:38,544
Sure, the monthly payments
would go up a little, but

94
00:05:38,594 --> 00:05:40,540
with a 30-year loan, I can make it work.

95
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,032
Ah,

96
00:05:42,082 --> 00:05:46,080
I still have the loan on the Jinsei Okuri Bunto,
the boat that sank.

97
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:48,461
The Jinsei Okuri Bunto?

98
00:05:48,511 --> 00:05:51,360
the cruiser I named for you

99
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:55,640
It ran aground on Motokatsu on its debut and sank,
didn't it?

100
00:05:57,380 --> 00:06:01,100
No way, I can't afford a
car this expensive after all.

101
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:03,200
So, giving up on auto camping,

102
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:05,900
just go have a barbecue
in your own backyard.

103
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:06,740
Sorry to keep you waiting.

104
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:09,800
Sorry, I think I'd rather
not go with a loan after all.

105
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:12,680
How about a rental car?

106
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:15,260
You have rental cars too?

107
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:17,660
Yes, please, have a look.

108
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:21,320
RVs like these are also very popular,

109
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:23,460
and we're renting them
at a reasonable price.

110
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:24,980
That sounds good.

111
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:28,120
The kids would probably love this one too.

112
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,400
Alright, I'll go with this one.

113
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:32,600
Boring.

114
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:34,300
Wait, Ryo-san.

115
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:39,360
You're just going to buy some cheap, flimsy
family camping set on sale, aren't you?

116
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:41,540
You don't need me at all, do you?

117
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:47,660
The car's a rental, but I plan to pick
out the camping gear one piece at a time.

118
00:06:47,660 --> 00:06:49,020
Please, Ryo-san.

119
00:06:50,460 --> 00:06:52,180
Then you'd better treat me to dinner too.

120
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:53,080
Fine.

121
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:56,880
Are we really going camping?

122
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:57,620
Awesome!

123
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,100
Of course, Daddy never lies.

124
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:01,480
Yay! Yay! Yay!

125
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:02,840
Camping, camping!

126
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,680
You have to write about
it in your summer diary.

127
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,800
Yeah! I will!

128
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:08,760
Alright, you two,
hurry up and go take your baths.

129
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:09,560
Okay!

130
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:13,480
Well, even after the
kids got out of the bath,

131
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:15,320
Don't let them into this room, okay?

132
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,740
What are you starting?

133
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:18,340
It's a rehearsal.

134
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:22,260
Apparently a lot of dads get flustered
once they get to the campsite, so.

135
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,760
Ryo-san, would you like seconds?

136
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:26,540
Heaped high, please.

137
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:28,720
Coming right up.

138
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:32,020
But it's so spacious here,
I'll feel unsettled going back home.

139
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:33,780
Here you go, Ryo-san.

140
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:35,220
Thanks.

141
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:38,680
There's still plenty of miso soup,
so please go ahead and have seconds.

142
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:45,300
In normal society, when someone
says they'll treat you to dinner,

143
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:48,580
they're usually angling to make a killing with some fancy scheme,
aren't they?

144
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:52,260
Says the guy who had three
extra helpings of rice!

145
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:53,820
Still, these characters are...

146
00:07:53,820 --> 00:08:02,300
I thought putting up a tent would be harder,

147
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:05,320
but the modern ones are so easy,
I'm surprised.

148
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:06,840
That's great, Terai-san.

149
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:10,180
With these,
I didn't even need to rely on Ryo-san.

150
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:10,940
Naive.

151
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:14,160
Indoors and at a campsite are different.

152
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:16,720
If you let your guard down,
you'll be in for a rough time.

153
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:18,100
I know, I know.

154
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:20,680
I'm also going to try
river fishing with the boys.

155
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,540
We'll catch and catch and catch!

156
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:23,160
There you go.

157
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:27,700
Just from watching fishing videos, you think
you're going to catch something, you fool.

158
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:29,320
You're so naive.

159
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:32,120
There's no tuna or bonito in the river,
you know.

160
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:33,840
I know that.

161
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,380
I'll grill the fish I catch
and share it with the kids,

162
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,380
munch munch,

163
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:39,940
it'll be delicious, won't it?

164
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:42,400
Terai, you're such a good dad.

165
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:45,160
I hate to rain on your parade,

166
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:47,340
but the campsite you're
going to is around here.

167
00:08:48,580 --> 00:08:50,580
It's raining. It might turn into a storm.

168
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,500
Oh my, that's terrible.

169
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,280
Just postpone it, Terai.

170
00:08:54,860 --> 00:08:56,000
It's fine, it's fine.

171
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,120
The weather forecast I saw this morning

172
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:00,160
said there's a 50% chance of rain,

173
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:03,420
and that the storm will
most likely veer off.

174
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:05,340
Are you really sure it'll be okay?

175
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:07,540
Senpai, what do you think?

176
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:08,560
Leave it alone.

177
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:11,340
This guy just doesn't get it.

178
00:09:11,340 --> 00:09:13,120
Ryo-chan, don't talk like that.

179
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:14,380
It'll be fine.

180
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:16,920
We'll blow any storm
away with sheer willpower.

181
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:17,820
Don't worry.

182
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:19,840
Here we go!

183
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:25,700
It's camping, camping! I'm so happy!

184
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:27,020
Are you okay?

185
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,400
Don't talk to me right now.

186
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:33,460
We've scheduled 15 minutes for
couple's talk at the next service area.

187
00:09:33,460 --> 00:09:38,560
If we don't follow the schedule, we won't
be able to get through everything, right?

188
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:40,900
Understood.

189
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:44,160
We absolutely have to keep to the schedule.

190
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:56,300
It's camping, camping! I'm so happy!

191
00:09:56,300 --> 00:09:58,860
Dad, you must be thirsty. Want some tea?

192
00:09:58,860 --> 00:10:01,780
We're planning to have tea
at the next service area.

193
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:18,360
Okay, it's ready!

194
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,140
Dad, you're amazing!

195
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:22,740
It's nothing!

196
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:25,920
All that practice paid off

197
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,400
Dad, I'm hungry!

198
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:37,020
Then let's go catch fish for dinner!

199
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:39,740
We're going now?

200
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:41,220
I'm already tired!

201
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:44,280
Tired already? We just got here.

202
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:47,100
Besides, at camp you do everything yourself.

203
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:49,060
Let's go, Kenji and Kouji!

204
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:49,960
Yes!

205
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:51,380
Be careful, okay?

206
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:56,800
Dammit!
Terai, after I taught him so persistently,

207
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:59,680
he's hammering the pegs
in the wrong direction!

208
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:00,640
Ryo-san?

209
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:03,616
Could it be...

210
00:11:03,666 --> 00:11:06,820
Did you come along because
you were worried about Terai?

211
00:11:07,180 --> 00:11:08,100
Hey, shh.

212
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:27,400
It's dangerous if you slip,
so stand back and watch Daddy fish.

213
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:29,720
I'd be fine with just curry rice.

214
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:31,800
Daddy, can you really catch fish?

215
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,020
Of course!

216
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:36,820
I've watched the fishing spot over
and over to visualize it for today.

217
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:38,540
I'm definitely going to catch one!

218
00:11:41,060 --> 00:11:41,560
Here it comes!

219
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:43,980
Daddy, you're amazing!

220
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:46,120
I'm going to fish too, after all!

221
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:46,840
Me too!

222
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:49,080
Alright, let's go fishing!

223
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:49,960
Yeah!

224
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:53,980
Ready, set, go!

225
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:54,340
Whoa!

226
00:11:57,260 --> 00:11:59,760
Oh no, the rod fell in!

227
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:03,660
Well, there's no help for it. Daddy will get it for you,
so hold on to this.

228
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:04,300
Okay.

229
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:06,840
Kenji, I'm counting on you
to handle the construction.

230
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,460
Okay. You be careful too, Daddy.

231
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:14,440
Good, I'm not being swept away.

232
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:15,260
Yoisho.

233
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:18,280
Whoa!

234
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:21,420
It's shallow.

235
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:26,180
Yoisho!

236
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:30,280
Phew, saved.

237
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:33,800
I caught another one!

238
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:35,040
Dad's amazing!

239
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:37,520
Yay, I caught it with my rod!

240
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:41,180
Let's say Koji caught this one.

241
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:43,800
Yay, we caught one, we caught one!

242
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:44,460
Hey, Dad!

243
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:45,120
Yo!

244
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:47,500
You've been struggling
with the tent all along!

245
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:49,720
Even if they still haven't noticed,

246
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:51,880
we've got to hurry up and finish fishing.

247
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:54,640
Wow, Dad, you're really good at fishing!

248
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:55,660
Apparently so.

249
00:12:55,660 --> 00:12:57,820
Dad, there's a bite!

250
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:59,700
Okay, slowly reel in the line...

251
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:01,140
Dad, me too!

252
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:03,120
Today's a big haul!

253
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:04,780
Dad's going to do his best too!

254
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:11,660
Look, look, Dad! You caught another one!

255
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:13,760
That's the tenth one!

256
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:15,940
Alright, now for Iwata!

257
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:17,720
Caught one!

258
00:13:20,820 --> 00:13:22,580
Dad, you caught so many!

259
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,520
Let's stop fishing here
and head back to the tent.

260
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:27,740
Mom's going to be so
surprised when she sees this!

261
00:13:27,740 --> 00:13:29,800
Yeah, we've got so many!

262
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:34,640
Catching that many,
are those guys planning to open a fish shop?

263
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:38,260
Still, Terai's pretty impressive
for not even noticing us.

264
00:13:38,260 --> 00:13:39,140
This is headquarters.

265
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:40,820
Ryo-chan, can you hear me?

266
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:43,820
This is the river fishing area, Ob...

267
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:48,000
Thanks for your hard work, Senpai Volvo.

268
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:50,340
I'm really worn out.

269
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:53,820
I reeled in all the fish I caught by hand.

270
00:13:53,820 --> 00:13:56,100
Come back quickly and have some coffee.

271
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:57,120
Roger.

272
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:59,860
At this rate,
the weather might just hold out.

273
00:14:00,660 --> 00:14:03,500
I guess Papa Terai's
determination beat the storm.

274
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:06,500
Yes, the kids are back.

275
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:08,960
Mommy, I caught lots of fish!

276
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:10,040
Wow, that's amazing!

277
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:13,820
Senpai Terai's kids are overjoyed!

278
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:16,020
I've had enough fish for a while, right?

279
00:14:16,020 --> 00:14:16,720
Me too.

280
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:19,520
That's strange, I can't see Terai anywhere.

281
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,080
Found him.

282
00:14:24,380 --> 00:14:25,740
What's he doing?

283
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:28,300
Ryo-chan, come back quickly.

284
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:30,300
Terai's started something again.

285
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:33,440
What's this?

286
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,680
It's a kamado.

287
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:37,200
You build a fire here and cook the rice.

288
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:40,240
Rice cooked in a kamado is incredibly delicious,
you know.

289
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:43,500
All you have to do now
is light the firewood.

290
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:49,360
Alright, everything's ready.

291
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:51,680
All that's left is cooking over the stove.

292
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:54,920
Dear, it looks like it's about to rain.
Will you be all right?

293
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:58,260
Yeah, I'm fine. I'm about to light it now.

294
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:02,220
Oh no, it broke.

295
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:05,360
Mommy, I'm hungry.

296
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:08,900
Daddy's building the stove right now, so

297
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:10,980
That's not going to work.

298
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:14,080
It's not a bath, so leave open
the side the wind is coming from.

299
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:15,900
We need to enclose the
remaining three sides,

300
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:17,420
I can't watch this.

301
00:15:17,420 --> 00:15:20,620
At this rate,
when are we ever going to get to eat?

302
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:22,460
Can't you even build a stove properly?

303
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:24,040
It's the most basic thing there is.

304
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:28,640
The kids are eating grass!

305
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:28,940
Maru~

306
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:32,340
Look, over there your
wife has the cup noodles

307
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:34,180
all ready to go.
What are you going to do, Terai?

308
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:38,160
Terai is trying to light the
firewood right off the bat!

309
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:39,240
Will it catch?

310
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,100
No way.

311
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:42,920
Didn't Terai buy solid fuel?

312
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:46,960
No, he should have brought
both solid fuel and charcoal.

313
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:48,640
Then why isn't he using them?

314
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:50,900
He's probably so excited
he forgot about them.

315
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:54,640
I kept insisting he buy a cartridge gas burner stove,
which is easy for beginners to use,

316
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:57,300
a two-burner stove,
and pushed him relentlessly.

317
00:15:57,780 --> 00:15:59,520
But then Terai went and

318
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:02,300
said, "It's too hard for beginners,
so just stick with a stove."

319
00:16:04,180 --> 00:16:09,500
Since we're going out to learn, I wanted to show
the kids how to light a fire in a stone stove.

320
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:13,320
Terai may look like that, but he's more
stubborn than Chief Ohara, you know.

321
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:14,360
It's bad!

322
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:16,550
What?

323
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:19,720
What on earth happened?

324
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:22,960
Looks like he dumped the gasoline and the
tea-roasting pot into the stove all at once.

325
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:25,860
That idiot, there's a limit
to how much you can improvise!

326
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:27,920
We've got an SOS signal from Mrs. Terai.

327
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:29,240
Where's the fire extinguisher?

328
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:32,240
Shouldn't we call 119?

329
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:35,220
Didn't we also need to spray water?

330
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:38,100
Sorry.

331
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:40,940
I never meant to put everyone in danger.

332
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:43,240
I just wanted the kids...

333
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:44,280
Hang in there!

334
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:45,940
We have to put out this fire quickly.

335
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:52,840
Keep moving upward 30 degrees.

336
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:54,540
OK.

337
00:16:56,540 --> 00:16:57,820
Pump's good to go.

338
00:16:58,280 --> 00:16:59,160
Roger.

339
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:00,940
Volvo-san, ready.

340
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:02,300
Roger.

341
00:17:06,160 --> 00:17:08,220
Dear, the fire's

342
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:15,140
starting to go out.

343
00:17:15,140 --> 00:17:18,420
Senpai, it's OK. Please pull up the pump.

344
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:20,140
Roger.

345
00:17:20,140 --> 00:17:20,400
No...

346
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:23,220
Volvo-san, operation complete.

347
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:24,260
Over.

348
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:33,700
All that good food...

349
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:35,680
The water will be boiling soon.

350
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:37,240
Let's eat cup noodles, dear.

351
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:39,880
Yay, I love cup noodles!

352
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:40,640
Hey, Koji.

353
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:43,760
Yeah, I didn't really want curry anyway.

354
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:46,400
Dear.

355
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:46,980
Dad.

356
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:49,760
And the fish you caught
got turned to charcoal.

357
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:53,240
I'm such a useless, unreliable father.

358
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:56,440
Terai's really dejected.

359
00:17:57,880 --> 00:18:00,480
We should be thankful it
didn't turn into a forest fire,

360
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:03,900
the smell of good curry
is coming from somewhere.

361
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:06,620
We decided on curry for dinner too.

362
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:08,400
Curry?

363
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:10,420
Wow, that looks delicious!

364
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:13,320
Hey, that's the same pot as Terai's,
isn't it?

365
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:15,260
It's Ryo-chan's recommendation.

366
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:17,080
I was sold one too.

367
00:18:17,080 --> 00:18:22,280
Are you making pocket money again by selling
pots you bought cheap somewhere at a high price?

368
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:24,500
Don't say such nasty things!

369
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:26,900
That's it, I've got a good idea!

370
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:28,400
What is it?

371
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,980
It's called the "Forest Animal Operation"!

372
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:34,760
Honey, let's eat some cup noodles.

373
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:36,080
Mm, yeah.

374
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:38,220
What is it?

375
00:18:41,060 --> 00:18:41,920
A b-bear!

376
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:44,280
A g-gorilla!

377
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:50,360
No, this is a crisis for our household!

378
00:18:50,380 --> 00:18:54,060
H-hey! I won't let you lay
a single finger on my family!

379
00:18:57,660 --> 00:18:58,220
This hand!

380
00:18:59,020 --> 00:19:00,620
Kana-kana-kana-kana-kana-kana!

381
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:02,720
Honey, run!

382
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:03,240
Daddy, that's amazing!

383
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:06,620
The food just didn't turn out right!
If you can eat it, go ahead and try!

384
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:07,080
Daddy!

385
00:19:07,140 --> 00:19:08,420
Honey, stop!

386
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:09,960
The wife next door

387
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:10,780
Daddy!

388
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:12,180
Reiko?

389
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:14,800
It's curry. Please share it with everyone.

390
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:18,920
Wait, so that one too, could it be...?

391
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:19,340
Yes.

392
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:22,320
Thank you. We'll gladly accept it.

393
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:27,600
Yay!

394
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:28,980
Yay!

395
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:30,740
Daddy!

396
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:31,660
Doria!

397
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:41,420
Volvo-san, the curry swap was a success!

398
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:43,960
Hey, Volvo, your butt's showing!

399
00:19:46,940 --> 00:19:48,940
We beat the gorilla and the grizzly bear!

400
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:54,360
We beat the gorilla and the grizzly bear!

401
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:55,120
Daddy!

402
00:19:56,020 --> 00:19:57,340
Daddy!

403
00:19:57,340 --> 00:19:59,060
Thank goodness, you're safe.

404
00:19:59,060 --> 00:20:00,020
Where's Mommy?

405
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:01,040
Over there.

406
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:02,800
Here you go.

407
00:20:05,260 --> 00:20:05,900
That's it.

408
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:09,500
All that sweating has made me hungry!

409
00:20:10,340 --> 00:20:12,460
Didn't we have curry just now...

410
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:14,980
Look! The first star!

411
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:18,900
Wow! It really is!

412
00:20:19,180 --> 00:20:20,520
Wow! The first star!

413
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:33,600
Damn it! Terai, that bastard!
He really went and hit me!

414
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:34,860
Got it!

415
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:35,705
Uh,

416
00:20:35,755 --> 00:20:38,980
Thanks to Terai, dinner's instant noodles

417
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:41,920
Try it.
It's military rations, but it's pretty good.

418
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:45,260
Looks like Terai and the
others have calmed down.

419
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:48,700
See, wasn't it worth coming camping?

420
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:49,500
Yeah.

421
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:53,000
Thanks, Dad and Mom.

422
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:55,280
It's nothing.

423
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,060
Dad, your face is red!

424
00:20:58,440 --> 00:20:59,620
That's not true.

425
00:21:03,340 --> 00:21:04,820
Got everything? Nothing forgotten?

426
00:21:04,820 --> 00:21:06,220
Alright, let's go.

427
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:08,120
Dad, I want to play more.

428
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:10,880
If we're late, the roads will be jammed.

429
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:14,320
We have to return the car by 5 PM, remember.

430
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:15,840
Hurry up and get in.

431
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:16,740
Coming!

432
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:23,660
Mom, can you check over there?

433
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:24,460
Okay.

434
00:21:24,460 --> 00:21:28,040
Honey, there's only about
five centimeters left!

435
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:28,480
What?

436
00:21:29,620 --> 00:21:29,800
Damn it!

437
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:37,040
Honey, the tire's about to fall off!

438
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:39,540
I-it's fine!

439
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:43,440
Honey, you need to back up first!

440
00:21:43,600 --> 00:21:44,460
I know!

441
00:21:46,500 --> 00:21:48,120
No good! It's dangerous!

442
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:49,840
We did it!

443
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:00,080
Are we floating?

444
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:06,320
That's...!

445
00:22:07,260 --> 00:22:08,040
Ryo-san!

446
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:10,520
Ryo-san! Everyone!

447
00:22:11,340 --> 00:22:12,600
Looks like we've been found out.

448
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:14,920
It's a hassle,
so I'll just carry it like this!

449
00:22:15,180 --> 00:22:18,900
Terai! I'll carry it all the way down,
so sit still and stay put!

450
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:25,320
Thanks, Ryo-san!
You happened to pass by, and you saved us!

451
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:27,480
Wow! It's flying!

452
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:30,040
Looks like they haven't
found out about yesterday.

453
00:22:30,040 --> 00:22:32,700
I'd rather just come clean about everything,
you know.

454
00:22:32,700 --> 00:22:34,140
Come on, let's hurry.

455
00:22:34,140 --> 00:22:36,280
We have to return the car by 5 o'clock.

456
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:40,880
Summer diary?

457
00:22:41,440 --> 00:22:41,840
Yeah.

458
00:22:42,340 --> 00:22:45,840
The kids' summer diaries came back,

459
00:22:45,840 --> 00:22:47,080
is there a problem?

460
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:48,780
Well, that's the thing.

461
00:22:49,600 --> 00:22:51,880
They wrote about catching
tons of river fish,

462
00:22:52,420 --> 00:22:56,320
the stove's fire going out
in a torrential downpour,

463
00:22:57,480 --> 00:22:59,080
throwing cars and a gorilla,

464
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,060
and getting dangling from a helicopter,
and so on.

465
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:04,840
Doesn't that sound like a fun diary?

466
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:08,600
But look here.

467
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:12,940
The teacher's comment says,
"Let's not write lies."

468
00:23:13,580 --> 00:23:16,380
Sure, they're all pretty fishy episodes,

469
00:23:16,380 --> 00:23:18,300
but it's all true, every bit of it.

470
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:19,220
Yeah, that's right.

471
00:23:19,220 --> 00:23:21,860
At least the last one, about the car,

472
00:23:21,860 --> 00:23:23,720
is something we actually did, right?

473
00:23:24,540 --> 00:23:25,260
Right.

474
00:23:25,980 --> 00:23:30,400
But after all that drawing, it's a shame to call it a lie.
The kids will feel bad.

475
00:23:30,920 --> 00:23:33,360
Okay, Terai.
How about this one for next time?

476
00:23:34,120 --> 00:23:39,060
In the winter break diary, I'll be Santa
and give you a ride in my flying sleigh!

477
00:24:01,080 --> 00:24:04,700
Sandals any time, scandals any time,
don't you mind them?

478
00:24:04,700 --> 00:24:05,520
No worries.

479
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:08,500
Cool play, every day.

480
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:09,680
Every day.

481
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:14,000
Boredom crumpled into a reprimand,
tossed away.

482
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:18,540
Bare instincts, raw instincts,
turning into fools.

483
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:19,480
Turning.

484
00:24:19,480 --> 00:24:22,340
Reckless and broke, so what's the harm?

485
00:24:22,340 --> 00:24:23,340
Isn't it?

486
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:28,120
Do what you want, just do it.

487
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:28,960
Amazing!

488
00:24:29,140 --> 00:24:30,940
The thunder of the stiff-necked chief.

489
00:24:30,940 --> 00:24:32,700
Smoke from the head.

490
00:24:33,600 --> 00:24:35,720
Run away and you'll be caught on camera

491
00:24:35,720 --> 00:24:36,160
On camera!

492
00:24:36,260 --> 00:24:37,480
Well, isn't that wonderful

493
00:24:37,480 --> 00:24:38,280
Ohoo

494
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:39,920
In the flowery Edo

495
00:24:39,920 --> 00:24:40,660
Hey there!

496
00:24:40,860 --> 00:24:41,940
Ryozan typhoon

497
00:24:41,940 --> 00:24:43,000
Thanks as always!

498
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:45,380
Raging wild

499
00:24:45,380 --> 00:24:47,600
Atarakamo play 9×2

500
00:24:47,600 --> 00:24:49,060
G game, G game

501
00:24:49,060 --> 00:24:51,360
Here's the water cut, lending, water fish

502
00:24:51,360 --> 00:24:53,960
Water fish, batsu eat, fish batsu eat

503
00:24:53,960 --> 00:24:55,240
Raibatsu eat, Derubatsu eat

504
00:25:03,900 --> 00:25:08,080
Thank you for watching

505
00:25:25,260 --> 00:25:26,600
This is truly golf, isn't it?

506
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:28,120
That was close!

507
00:25:29,040 --> 00:25:31,300
Next time: deserted island golf

508
00:25:31,300 --> 00:25:32,120
See you, okay?

